+### 1. Important — flaky `distinctWorkersUsed > 1` heuristic
+
+**Closed, verified independently, not just re-read.** The old heuristic (and its `perWorkerTouches` bookkeeping) is deleted outright, not merely relaxed — the 10k-item test now only checks the exact-once-touch property. The replacement is a genuinely deterministic barrier proof: `Scheduler::create(2)` (explicit, `REQUIRE(workerCount() == 2)`, gated defensively again on `< 2` inside the test), then `parallelFor(2, 1, fn)` where each of the 2 dispatched units (`REQUIRE(end - begin == 1)` defensively enforces one unit each) increments a shared `arrived` atomic and then spins on `std::this_thread::yield()` — **not** a nested `parallelFor`/`WaitforTask()` call — until it observes `arrived == 2`, bounded by a 20s per-unit wall-clock deadline that sets a `timeouts` flag and returns instead of spinning forever.
