+Traced why this can only pass under genuine concurrency: the spin-wait is a plain busy-loop with no call back into enkiTS's dispatch machinery, so — unlike the nested-`parallelFor` test — there is no cooperative "run other pending work while I wait" escape hatch available to the thread executing either unit. A single OS thread cannot pause itself mid-callback on its own initiative to go run the other unit; the only way `arrived` can ever reach 2 is if two genuinely distinct threads are each independently making progress within the same 20s window. Confirmed the timeout path fails loud rather than hanging: `REQUIRE(timeouts.load() == 0)` converts any timeout into an immediate, bounded (≤ ~20s) test failure, not an infinite wait — the harness can never hang on this test.
